Observability only. This adds no capability and changes no result; it exists so a
stalled graph_compute says where it stopped.

Why it is needed. When a real MoE model is run on a WebGPU RPC peer, graph_compute
does not return and neither side prints anything at all (docs/CONSTRAINTS.md O11).
That silence is structural, not incidental:

    ggml-webgpu.cpp, ggml_backend_webgpu_wait()
        while (blocking_wait) {
            waitStatus = instance.WaitAny(1, &subs[0].submit_done, 100ms);
            if (handle_wait_status(waitStatus, true)) { ... subs.erase(...); }
            blocking_wait = (block && !subs.empty()) || ...;
        }

handle_wait_status returns false for TimedOut (silently, when allow_timeout is set)
and false for Error (after logging), and neither erases the submission - so either
status spins at 10 Hz forever while graph_compute never returns.

What it separates. Encoding, the selected node metadata/pipeline path, an intermediate
submit, the final completion wait, and the WaitAny status are different observations that
currently look identical from the outside:

    graph_compute begin n_nodes=N
    encode node=i/N op=...            before encoding node i, every
                                      GGML_WEBGPU_TRACE_STRIDE nodes
                                      (default 64), and the last one
    submit #k after node=i kernels=n
    wait(partial|final) begin subs=k
    wait(partial) poll status=... subs_before=k subs_after=k|k-1
    WaitAny #n status=TimedOut|Error|Unknown      (blocking loop only)
    wait(partial|final) end retries=n subs=k
    mul_mat path=vec|fast|legacy pipeline=...
    build_multi[...] param_alloc|bind_group|encoder|dispatch|finish ...
    graph_compute end

Deliberate choices:

  - Off unless GGML_WEBGPU_TRACE is set in the environment. A build can then be
    carried to the machine where the stall reproduces and switched on there, instead
    of being rebuilt there. The Runtime adapter passes it through Module.ENV, the
    same way it already sets NO_COLOR.
  - Nodes are logged every 64 by default, not every node: thousands of lines would
    make the logging itself a plausible reason the timing changed.
  - WaitAny retries are thinned to 1, 10, 50, then every 100 up to 1000, then every
    1000 - roughly immediately, 1 s, 5 s, every 10 s, then every 100 s at the 100 ms
    timeout. **A change of status is always reported regardless of thinning**, because
    spinning on TimedOut and spinning on Error are different faults and the thinning
    would otherwise hide the moment one becomes the other.

GGML_WEBGPU_TRACE_STRIDE narrows that once a stall is known to sit inside one of
those windows: set it to 1 and the last line names the node. Too noisy to leave on,
and useless before there is a window to narrow, which is why it is not the default.

This is not a Qwen3.6 compatibility patch and nothing depends on it. If O11 is
resolved without it, drop it.

